  "name": "alexandria-common",
  "description": "Alexandria-common serves as the shared data model layer for the Alexandria library management system, defining core schemas for inventory, users, and transaction history. It implements serializable domain objects and enums to represent library actions and permission levels, facilitating consistent data exchange across the project's ecosystem. The implementation focuses on mapping application-level logic to relational database primitives using early Rust serialization patterns.",
